Tasks

1. Open MongoDB shell and create a new database named insta_clone_db, then switch to it using the appropriate commands.

-> use insta_clone_db


2. Inside insta_clone_db, create a collection called posts that will store Instagram-style photo posts.

-> db.createCollection("posts")


3. Create another collection named stories in insta_clone_db, and insert a sample story document with fields: username, image_url, and timestamp.

->  db.createCollection("stories")
->  db.stories.insertOne({
        username: "meet_parmar",
        image_url: "https://example.com/story.jpg",
        timestamp: new Date()
    })


4. Drop the stories collection from insta_clone_db and verify that it no longer exists.

-> db.stories.drop()
-> show collections


5. Drop the entire insta_clone_db database from MongoDB, then use the show dbs command to confirm it has been deleted.

-> db.dropDatabase()
-> show dbs